#question(title: [Sphere])[
  You know the formula for the volume of a
  sphere with radius $R$. Now you are able to
  prove it!

  + Write an equation for the circle with
    radius $R$ centered at $(0, 0)$.
  + If you rotate this circle around the
    $x$-axis, it will produce a sphere.
    Compute its volume as an integral by
    slicing it like a carrot.
]
